  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "McDaniel College Budapest, founded in 1994, stands as a fully accredited American college nestled in the heart of Europe. Born from the visionary aspirations of McDaniel College alumnus George Varga, the Budapest campus embodies a commitment to enriching Hungary's higher education landscape with a liberal arts presence. Over the years, the institution has evolved, now offering a comprehensive four-year Bachelor's Degree program, aiming to deliver the pinnacle of U.S. higher learning amidst the dynamic international setting of Budapest.\n\nHere are some of the popular undergraduate and graduate programs that McDaniel offers.\n\nUndergraduate Programs: McDaniel College offers a wide range of undergraduate programs across various disciplines, including arts and humanities, social sciences, natural sciences, business, and education. Prospective undergraduate students can choose from bachelor's degrees, minors, and pre-professional programs designed to meet their academic and career interests.\n\nGraduate Programs: While McDaniel College primarily focuses on undergraduate education, it does offer a limited number of postgraduate programs, including master's degrees in fields such as teaching and counseling. These programs provide opportunities for advanced study and professional development in specialized areas.\n\nAdmission to undergraduate programs at McDaniel College is competitive and typically requires meeting specific academic criteria, including a minimum GPA, standardized test scores (SAT or ACT), letters of recommendation, and a personal statement. International students may also need to demonstrate proficiency in English through tests like the TOEFL or IELTS."
